1. **PART A, RD-1002, commit A, `__tests__/rd969-three-routes-empty-request.test.js` only, comment lines only.** The header says "The cells run" (no count) and adds one sentence saying the index names every cell and carries no count; the index gains H6, H7 and H8 in its own two-column form. **a-pred** (a program, no jest, run at base and at head by you; the text is frozen here): `python3 -I -B` over the raw file, cells = ids of the `test('<id>:` lines, index = ids in the header text before the first `*/`; passes only when `cells - index` is empty. Expected: base `H6 H7 H8`, head none. Control: delete `H8` from the head's header copy in scratch and the program reports `H8`. Only comment lines may differ (a program: the added and removed lines all start with ` * ` inside the header block). The a-pred program (frozen; it was run by the drafter on the base file and on the patched copy: base prints the three missing ids, head prints none):
```python
import re, sys
t = open(sys.argv[1], encoding='utf8').read()
cells = set(re.findall(r"^\s*test\('([A-Z]\d?b?):", t, re.M))
hdr = t[:t.index('*/')]
idx = set(re.findall(r"(?:^ \* |   )([MHE]\d+b?) ", hdr, re.M))
print(sorted(cells - idx))
sys.exit(1 if cells - idx else 0)
```
